    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0565" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.071 Control/200</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Embassy to the
                            Department of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p>Upon the occasion of the presentation and subsequent hearings before the House
                    Immigration and Naturalization Committee during the past month of the Schulte
                    Bill (H. R. 5380) and of the hearings which are now taking place before the
                    Senate Immigration Committee on the King Bill (S. 379), the Italian Embassy
                    would again respectfully point out the remarks made in previous memorandums
                    addressed to the United States Department of State, particularly in the one of
                    March 6th 1934.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d349-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>It is believed that these Bills, dealing on the deportation of alien seamen, if
                    enacted into law, would not allow a desirable cooperation in matters of shipping
                    between the United States and Italy, as pointed out in the memorandum above
                    mentioned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-04-10">April 10,
                            1935</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
